<title>GERMANY: Toepfer keeps 1997 grain area forecast unchanged.</title>
<headline>Toepfer keeps 1997 grain area forecast unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union grain area in 1997 should be expanded to 37.2 million hectares from 36.4 million in 1996, grain trader Alfred C Toepfer said in its latest monthly market newsletter.</p>
<p>Toepfer kept its April area estimate unchanged but this time did not comment on the possible size of the crop, which last month it had put at 205 million tonnes (201 million in 1996).</p>
<p>Rains in recent weeks had improved crop prospects but Spain and Portugal were still too dry, Toepfer said.</p>
<p>Average grain yields in the EU this year should therefore be below those achieved in the 1996 harvest.</p>
<p>-Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
